<title>UK: Colombia declines OPEC membership - minister.</title>
<headline>Colombia declines OPEC membership - minister.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia declined an invitation to join the Organisation for Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC), Colombia's Minister of Mines and Energy Rodrigo Villa Mizar said on Monday.</p>
<p>Asked if he had been approached by the organisation, he said &quot;Yes, we have and we don't intend to become a member of OPEC.</p>
<p>&quot;We think there is a lot more flexibilty in our operation. I think the non-OPEC market is growing faster. It's probably the only one that is really growing now.&quot;</p>
<p>Colombia's oil production of 630,000 barrels per day (bpd) is expected to rise to 900,000 bpd by the beginning of 1998, the minister said.</p>
<p>-- Tom Ashby, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
